WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 4 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:12.104
Training policy: bill only verified worked hours; use DEL for delivery and TRN for training; any overtime needs the specified approval evidence before

00:00:12.104 --> 00:00:13.531
supervisor approval.

00:00:13.771 --> 00:00:18.464
This is a fictional policy, not an SAP rule or employment-law instruction.

00:00:19.154 --> 00:00:29.821
Use this evidence packet: Monday 8 DEL; Tuesday 8 DEL; Wednesday 6 DEL plus 2 TRN; Thursday 8 DEL; Friday 6 DEL.

00:00:30.061 --> 00:00:32.813
The verified weekly total is 38 hours.

00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:38.002
TS-104 instead shows 8 DEL each weekday, totaling 40.

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:40.761
Worked review: first compare dates.

00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:42.537
Monday and Tuesday agree.

00:00:42.777 --> 00:00:46.745
Wednesday’s total of 8 agrees, but 2 hours are on the wrong task.

00:00:46.985 --> 00:00:48.073
Thursday agrees.

00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:50.489
Friday is overstated by 2 hours.

00:00:50.729 --> 00:00:55.423
The correct breakdown is 36 DEL and 2 TRN, totaling 38.

00:00:55.663 --> 00:01:00.612
A total-only check would miss Wednesday’s coding error even if Friday had been corrected.

00:01:01.302 --> 00:01:05.398
Treat discrepancies as questions about evidence, not proof of intent.

00:01:05.638 --> 00:01:11.569
If source records disagree, pause the decision and ask the responsible person for clarification.

00:01:11.809 --> 00:01:16.438
Do not invent a reason for the difference or silently adjust someone else’s time.

00:01:16.678 --> 00:01:20.454
Record only the minimum factual detail needed for correction.

00:01:21.144 --> 00:01:22.232
Now it's your turn.

00:01:22.472 --> 00:01:27.165
The weekly total is corrected to 38, but Wednesday still shows 8 DEL.

00:01:27.405 --> 00:01:28.195
What now?

00:01:28.435 --> 00:01:31.549
